*(rustc)* stop warning and leaking blobs when another checkout already\npublished a key ([#719](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/719))\n- *(build-script)* remove a collected OUT_DIR tree all or nothing\n([#712](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/712))\n- *(cli)* answer ConPTY's cursor position request so builds start on\nWindows ([#709](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/709))\n- *(build-script)* reuse of outputs that embed a canonicalized OUT_DIR\n([#711](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/711))\n- *(cc)* stop the C shim recursing when ccache is on PATH\n([#707](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/pull/707))\n</blockquote>\n\n## `mbx-cache-cargo`\n\n<blockquote>\n\n##\n[0.3.14](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/compare/mbx-cache-cargo-v0.3.13...mbx-cache-cargo-v0.3.14)\n- 2026-10-15\n\n### Other\n\n- updated the following local packages: mbx-cache-core\n</blockquote>\n\n## `mbx-cache-store`\n\n<blockquote>\n\n##\n[0.1.40](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/compare/mbx-cache-store-v0.1.39...mbx-cache-store-v0.1.40)\n- 2026-10-15\n\n### Other\n\n- updated the following local packages: mbx-cache-core\n</blockquote>\n\n\n</p></details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with\n[release-plz](https://github.com/release-plz/release-plz/).\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Mechanical version and changelog updates only; behavioral changes were\nmerged in earlier PRs and are already covered by those reviews.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **Release-only PR** (release-plz): bumps crate versions, refreshes\nchangelogs, updates `Cargo.lock`, and sets the documented CLI version to\n**1.24.1**. No application source changes appear in this diff.\n> \n> **Versions:** `mbx` 1.24.0 → 1.24.1; `mbx-cache-core`, `mbx-cache-cc`,\nand `mbx-cache-rustc` 0.20.1 → 0.20.2; `mbx-cache-cargo` 0.3.13 →\n0.3.14; `mbx-cache-store` 0.1.39 → 0.1.40. Dependent crates pin the new\n`mbx-cache-core` release.\n> \n> **What ships in 1.24.1** (from changelog entries added here): rustc\ncache fixes when another checkout already published a key; build-script\n`OUT_DIR` collection and reuse; Windows ConPTY cursor handling so builds\nstart; C shim no longer recurses when `ccache` is on `PATH`.\n**`mbx-cache-rustc` 0.20.2** also documents PGO compile reuse and\ncaching for `-C linker-flavor` rlibs/checks.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n0663751ca7004fb815e869dc6884170a7d287647. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-16T10:19:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/ebb2b61b193d9ea487b67152d459e8332e8cf87e","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/commit/ebb2b61b193d9ea487b67152d459e8332e8cf87e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/ebb2b61b193d9ea487b67152d459e8332e8cf87e/comments","author":{"login":"jdx","id":216188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjE4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b7aabce346c619a348d9d7c9403d0343f251d84f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/b7aabce346c619a348d9d7c9403d0343f251d84f","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/commit/b7aabce346c619a348d9d7c9403d0343f251d84f"}]},"status":"ahead","ahead_by":29,"behind_by":0,"total_commits":29,"commits":[{"sha":"544db435c055d4a4fe25eb5e7a4fc70adcfea261","node_id":"C_kwDOT-nLJdoAKDU0NGRiNDM1YzA1NWQ0YTRmZTI1ZWI1ZTdhNGZjNzBhZGNmZWEyNjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonathan Ellis","email":"jbellis@gmail.com","date":"2026-10-16T13:25:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-16T13:25:17Z"},"message":"fix(scheduler): prevent starvation across shared container builds (#721)\n\nConcurrent builds sharing a cache can indefinitely postpone a large\ncompilation: each newly arriving small job takes capacity before the\nolder request can accumulate enough permits. This change queues\nadmission requests so older eligible work gets a turn, while requests\nblocked by their own build or container do not stop unrelated\ncontainers.\n\nWhen a shared cache is configured with a host-sized CPU/memory budget,\nadmission also respects each container's local CPU and memory ceiling.\nLease records carry their memory unit so processes using different\nbudget settings are accounted for conservatively during a configuration\ntransition. Waiter records are kernel-locked and disappear from\nadmission ordering after cancellation or process death, including when a\nrecord is removed while another process is scanning the queue.\nShared-cache operators should explicitly configure the common host\nbudget as described in `docs/scheduling.md`; defaults remain local to\neach process.\n\nValidation: 69 scheduler tests and 159 targeted\nbuild/Cargo/nextest/session/storage integration tests passed, plus\nall-target/all-feature Clippy. Separate process and two-container\nreproductions verified starvation prevention, cancellation cleanup, and\nprogress in another container while one container is full. A portable\nrelease is deployed to the affected shared host. The full library run\nhad an unchanged renderer assertion failure\n(`mascot_keeps_progress_readable_and_leaves_successful_builds`, expected\nRGB sequence); a header-snapshot test failed once and passed on retry.\n\nFull `mise run ci` failed: the library suite reported 929 passed, 2\nfailed (`successful_before_snapshots_still_detect_new_headers` and the\nrenderer assertion above), and 1 ignored. Bats also reported `a make\nbuild's C objects restore into a second checkout` failing (reproduced in\nan isolated retry); the remaining CI tasks were interrupted when the\nlibrary task failed. Documentation generation/checks, links, interactive\nterminal checks, debug Clippy, and the release diagnostic test passed.\nThese failures are outside the changed scheduler code; this PR does not\nclaim a green full gate.\n\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Codex; model: OpenAI/unavailable; version:\nunavailable.*\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Claude Code; model: Anthropic/claude-opus-5-5;\nversion: 2.1.300.*\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Compilation requests that cannot fit retain their place ahead of newer\neligible requests, which cannot consume the capacity they need.\n* Scheduling enforces host-wide, pressure-domain, per-build, and\nmachine-capacity limits, including memory-based limits.\n* Waiters release their queue position when cancelled or blocked by\nsupervision, resource pressure, or memory checks.\n* **Documentation**\n* Expanded guidance on shared-cache container budgets, scheduling\nlimits, and wrapper upgrades for ordered admission.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a06e2029aa475bce692c203eb917ce870a5119d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/git/trees/a06e2029aa475bce692c203eb917ce870a5119d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/git/commits/544db435c055d4a4fe25eb5e7a4fc70adcfea261","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq0iW9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJLEQAHaEqzZbU42azZMQr67ev9Td\nCndHgCc10smnUQGDRUC2CrYC2AoBNPG8KzlOQHFfiLn1g41zvY2B5qjb7ZWKgGtc\nSeJw70CE8IU3qOnsicZn2uPBJ//q8PlrGrf4A9U4TzZjwvPtDkZKV8AkKA/vRJsh\nnDJWwhW7LyYLfNpsu7N0bjX948MA493PgOtemsdZVZAVC/D8TO6E846ff8OL3BRh\nXohxqXhT774QqiotK62/fIyoG0UFHvZekgC8dimUmAIJ9LqbU/oj4+YA5kTK8iew\n3x5oK6Swe9qlHDJI4W2WbWo13kcGLITx35ewHcDRYSnjU/zua8lP8IEqBbFuzlkK\n4FY5AtznCTJW/krkYSOXUPXR0JKotuAnFkg38sd0OgVl59Lieu467cEdIsJ5vGhq\n9eyWZNQsLUJ+cJEN+RcmxFrYnz5yy9IRVBx5CUgn08hSnnrP/ZOPSsSnHp0EISIE\n/Mo8W3KbdFGktngankFs551nz1KwsXw9lqYpRPGz8tp/e7aUl3r05P50yy5Wtbw5\nVrW34VTozrjUk/TDvKY4M0paDz5c6B5t26xZqbm4LrPffK2SIKjloCSFnEg99Fbp\n4aW+gz/V82urmPFFNOisyPvQPx85MlRO69yhP0EpdDyumawT6/BLDQATrE2zSB4l\nOyCBwtzJilO9oW0Dyw4X\n=kKRD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a06e2029aa475bce692c203eb917ce870a5119d2\nparent ebb2b61b193d9ea487b67152d459e8332e8cf87e\nauthor Jonathan Ellis <jbellis@gmail.com> 1792157117 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792157117 -0500\n\nfix(scheduler): prevent starvation across shared container builds (#721)\n\nConcurrent builds sharing a cache can indefinitely postpone a large\ncompilation: each newly arriving small job takes capacity before the\nolder request can accumulate enough permits. This change queues\nadmission requests so older eligible work gets a turn, while requests\nblocked by their own build or container do not stop unrelated\ncontainers.\n\nWhen a shared cache is configured with a host-sized CPU/memory budget,\nadmission also respects each container's local CPU and memory ceiling.\nLease records carry their memory unit so processes using different\nbudget settings are accounted for conservatively during a configuration\ntransition. Waiter records are kernel-locked and disappear from\nadmission ordering after cancellation or process death, including when a\nrecord is removed while another process is scanning the queue.\nShared-cache operators should explicitly configure the common host\nbudget as described in `docs/scheduling.md`; defaults remain local to\neach process.\n\nValidation: 69 scheduler tests and 159 targeted\nbuild/Cargo/nextest/session/storage integration tests passed, plus\nall-target/all-feature Clippy. Separate process and two-container\nreproductions verified starvation prevention, cancellation cleanup, and\nprogress in another container while one container is full. A portable\nrelease is deployed to the affected shared host. The full library run\nhad an unchanged renderer assertion failure\n(`mascot_keeps_progress_readable_and_leaves_successful_builds`, expected\nRGB sequence); a header-snapshot test failed once and passed on retry.\n\nFull `mise run ci` failed: the library suite reported 929 passed, 2\nfailed (`successful_before_snapshots_still_detect_new_headers` and the\nrenderer assertion above), and 1 ignored. Bats also reported `a make\nbuild's C objects restore into a second checkout` failing (reproduced in\nan isolated retry); the remaining CI tasks were interrupted when the\nlibrary task failed. Documentation generation/checks, links, interactive\nterminal checks, debug Clippy, and the release diagnostic test passed.\nThese failures are outside the changed scheduler code; this PR does not\nclaim a green full gate.\n\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Codex; model: OpenAI/unavailable; version:\nunavailable.*\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Claude Code; model: Anthropic/claude-opus-5-5;\nversion: 2.1.300.*\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Compilation requests that cannot fit retain their place ahead of newer\neligible requests, which cannot consume the capacity they need.\n* Scheduling enforces host-wide, pressure-domain, per-build, and\nmachine-capacity limits, including memory-based limits.\n* Waiters release their queue position when cancelled or blocked by\nsupervision, resource pressure, or memory checks.\n* **Documentation**\n* Expanded guidance on shared-cache container budgets, scheduling\nlimits, and wrapper upgrades for ordered admission.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-16T13:25:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/544db435c055d4a4fe25eb5e7a4fc70adcfea261","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/commit/544db435c055d4a4fe25eb5e7a4fc70adcfea261","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/544db435c055d4a4fe25eb5e7a4fc70adcfea261/comments","author":{"login":"jbellis","id":42158,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMTU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42158?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbellis","html_url":"https://github.com/jbellis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbellis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbellis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbellis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbellis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbellis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbellis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbellis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbellis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbellis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ebb2b61b193d9ea487b67152d459e8332e8cf87e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/ebb2b61b193d9ea487b67152d459e8332e8cf87e","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/commit/ebb2b61b193d9ea487b67152d459e8332e8cf87e"}]},{"sha":"0423391d49a1d2eecb976b1b25ed51cd76de7f0c","node_id":"C_kwDOT-nLJdoAKDA0MjMzOTFkNDlhMWQyZWVjYjk3NmIxYjI1ZWQ1MWNkNzZkZTdmMGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jdx","email":"216188+jdx@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-16T14:05:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-16T14:05:17Z"},"message":"feat(cache): add remote.trust_writes for CI systems mbx does not detect (#724)\n\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/jdx/mr-boxington/trails/177\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\nmbx only lets GitHub Actions and GitLab CI push builds write to a remote\ncache. On any other CI (Buildkite, Jenkins, and so on),\n`MBX_REMOTE_MODE=read-write` silently acts as `read-only`, so the bucket\nstays empty. This was reported against Buildkite in #722.\n\n`remote.trust_writes` (`MBX_REMOTE_TRUST_WRITES=true`) skips that policy\nand uses `remote.mode` as configured. It defaults to false, so GitHub\nActions and GitLab CI behave as before. Rather than add a detection rule\nper CI vendor, the pipeline owner decides which builds are trusted,\nusing their CI's own conditions:\n\n```sh\n# Buildkite agent environment hook\nif [ \"$BUILDKITE_BRANCH\" = \"$BUILDKITE_PIPELINE_DEFAULT_BRANCH\" ] \\\n  && [ \"$BUILDKITE_PULL_REQUEST\" = false ]; then\n  export MBX_REMOTE_TRUST_WRITES=true\nfi\n```\n\n`mbx doctor` then shows `configured read-write, effective read-write`.\n\nThe setting disables the guard entirely, so the docs say to set it only\nfrom the agent or pipeline environment, never from a file a pull request\ncan edit, and to limit the write credential to the same builds.\n`remote.mode` is unchanged: `write-only` stays write-only and\n`read-only` stays read-only when the setting is on.\n\nTested with a unit test covering all three modes in a local shell and a\nGitHub pull request, plus the existing policy, config and doctor unit\ntests. Not tested against a live Buildkite pipeline.\n\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Claude Code; model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5;\nversion: unavailable.*\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Opt-in flag disables client-side remote-cache write policy entirely\nwhen enabled, so misconfiguration (e.g. in PR-controlled env) could\nallow untrusted cache publishes; defaults and workspace rejection limit\nexposure.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Adds **`remote.trust_writes`** (`MBX_REMOTE_TRUST_WRITES`, default\n`false`) so operators on CI mbx does not recognize (Buildkite, Jenkins,\netc.) can opt out of the client-side write guard and honor\n**`remote.mode`** as configured instead of treating `read-write` as\nread-only.\n> \n> **Policy:** `effective_remote_cache_mode` now takes `trust_writes`;\nwhen true it bypasses GitHub/GitLab trusted-writer detection (including\non PRs and local shells). **`mbx doctor`** and remote cache setup use\nthe same resolution.\n> \n> **Safety:** Workspace **`.mbx.toml` cannot set** `[remote]` /\n`trust_writes` (new test); docs stress setting it only from trusted\nagent/pipeline env and scoping write credentials.\n> \n> **Tests:** Policy unit test for `trust_writes` across all three modes\nin untrusted contexts; existing policy tests updated for the new\nparameter.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n982a7e110b7685914d12e4b9cadd60ab50029852. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added an opt-in setting to allow remote-cache writes when the usual CI\ntrust policy would restrict them. It is disabled by default, can be set\nthrough an environment variable, and is not accepted in workspace\nconfiguration.\n  * Remote-cache diagnostics now reflect the effective write policy.\n* **Documentation**\n* Clarified remote-cache write permissions for CI systems, with guidance\non trusted environments and an example for enabling writes on a\nprotected default branch.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jacob <76940960+THEjacob1000@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f1e7c1b1406d466712f68412826fc415b91a92c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/git/trees/9f1e7c1b1406d466712f68412826fc415b91a92c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/git/commits/0423391d49a1d2eecb976b1b25ed51cd76de7f0c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq0i8dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvKcQAJtw4rpAQBTKjiUISpuSNIhP\n2N2HQVXlGLFdg3H527HQQlvvdO0tn8hH2TsVS8rPLq+4x6Fs1jCeLQ11TEN8h07s\ncmnyrtrQTGAnKppvO+nfnbz9RHcuUEF63+5lSjkiuGDhidfJMqm0vlfkVqS7DfXl\nScFh0GBoGLIiZtRu3m9xpW1tJFeHmExp+6xV+15VK0eklUbLeRANJKqJDSSdqN50\nlnFspA90vtl31u3KI3Mii8JQCQmYZ2Agb74GLbLwv9KIth8dtYgdXS0cwpuJ8b1D\nIZsW7w3Eb5XZ/QVchU8QAzUIE2Yr2qRaJV2lKDRqURR4ojFopT8awiOLzeNbRzfh\nBvA+LayF8ObzjfAXM5gtHliR4pW6KuinmzyRdR1Npf++uH3Ly1XrzTy9pMs8/E2k\nTUP+LO6MWZjAq9M1nXNR0JzfXtm3ShlPB0QLE9JLvEpbL9nvb9s2sR2Hp8kOMVPf\nudAmVlcPe62g8iJvmL+Db4DtlRs4h2ngMjfrQ/IZEFmDkVvq6hP2b/kzsmq5ZrSV\npVlF/VmyutxOqxJRgnmKazdGXXedX1pzMLlMt7C81DhPYopmcS0DSW4qny+JEpof\n9erDhL+S132TCy4YtewI3cOnl3FR7tEFx3LFAvKjkJaWfnU8/zcta2SW0u1xD6jt\nBNqj/SGPsDVUMXD84pm1\n=7fQv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9f1e7c1b1406d466712f68412826fc415b91a92c\nparent 544db435c055d4a4fe25eb5e7a4fc70adcfea261\nauthor jdx <216188+jdx@users.noreply.github.com> 1792159517 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792159517 -0500\n\nfeat(cache): add remote.trust_writes for CI systems mbx does not detect (#724)\n\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/jdx/mr-boxington/trails/177\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\nmbx only lets GitHub Actions and GitLab CI push builds write to a remote\ncache. On any other CI (Buildkite, Jenkins, and so on),\n`MBX_REMOTE_MODE=read-write` silently acts as `read-only`, so the bucket\nstays empty. This was reported against Buildkite in #722.\n\n`remote.trust_writes` (`MBX_REMOTE_TRUST_WRITES=true`) skips that policy\nand uses `remote.mode` as configured. It defaults to false, so GitHub\nActions and GitLab CI behave as before. Rather than add a detection rule\nper CI vendor, the pipeline owner decides which builds are trusted,\nusing their CI's own conditions:\n\n```sh\n# Buildkite agent environment hook\nif [ \"$BUILDKITE_BRANCH\" = \"$BUILDKITE_PIPELINE_DEFAULT_BRANCH\" ] \\\n  && [ \"$BUILDKITE_PULL_REQUEST\" = false ]; then\n  export MBX_REMOTE_TRUST_WRITES=true\nfi\n```\n\n`mbx doctor` then shows `configured read-write, effective read-write`.\n\nThe setting disables the guard entirely, so the docs say to set it only\nfrom the agent or pipeline environment, never from a file a pull request\ncan edit, and to limit the write credential to the same builds.\n`remote.mode` is unchanged: `write-only` stays write-only and\n`read-only` stays read-only when the setting is on.\n\nTested with a unit test covering all three modes in a local shell and a\nGitHub pull request, plus the existing policy, config and doctor unit\ntests. Not tested against a live Buildkite pipeline.\n\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Claude Code; model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5;\nversion: unavailable.*\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Opt-in flag disables client-side remote-cache write policy entirely\nwhen enabled, so misconfiguration (e.g. in PR-controlled env) could\nallow untrusted cache publishes; defaults and workspace rejection limit\nexposure.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Adds **`remote.trust_writes`** (`MBX_REMOTE_TRUST_WRITES`, default\n`false`) so operators on CI mbx does not recognize (Buildkite, Jenkins,\netc.) can opt out of the client-side write guard and honor\n**`remote.mode`** as configured instead of treating `read-write` as\nread-only.\n> \n> **Policy:** `effective_remote_cache_mode` now takes `trust_writes`;\nwhen true it bypasses GitHub/GitLab trusted-writer detection (including\non PRs and local shells). **`mbx doctor`** and remote cache setup use\nthe same resolution.\n> \n> **Safety:** Workspace **`.mbx.toml` cannot set** `[remote]` /\n`trust_writes` (new test); docs stress setting it only from trusted\nagent/pipeline env and scoping write credentials.\n> \n> **Tests:** Policy unit test for `trust_writes` across all three modes\nin untrusted contexts; existing policy tests updated for the new\nparameter.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n982a7e110b7685914d12e4b9cadd60ab50029852. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added an opt-in setting to allow remote-cache writes when the usual CI\ntrust policy would restrict them. It is disabled by default, can be set\nthrough an environment variable, and is not accepted in workspace\nconfiguration.\n  * Remote-cache diagnostics now reflect the effective write policy.\n* **Documentation**\n* Clarified remote-cache write permissions for CI systems, with guidance\non trusted environments and an example for enabling writes on a\nprotected default branch.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jacob <76940960+THEjacob1000@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-16T14:05:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/0423391d49a1d2eecb976b1b25ed51cd76de7f0c","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/commit/0423391d49a1d2eecb976b1b25ed51cd76de7f0c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/0423391d49a1d2eecb976b1b25ed51cd76de7f0c/comments","author":{"login":"jdx","id":216188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjE4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"544db435c055d4a4fe25eb5e7a4fc70adcfea261","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/544db435c055d4a4fe25eb5e7a4fc70adcfea261","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/commit/544db435c055d4a4fe25eb5e7a4fc70adcfea261"}]},{"sha":"2436db43982689b99b9a0e5794919398404e034f","node_id":"C_kwDOT-nLJdoAKDI0MzZkYjQzOTgyNjg5Yjk5YjlhMGU1Nzk0OTE5Mzk4NDA0ZTAzNGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jdx","email":"216188+jdx@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-16T23:33:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-16T23:33:08Z"},"message":"ci: pin perf-runner image by tag and stop automerging it (#725)\n\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/jdx/mr-boxington/trails/178\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\nRenovate's runs on this repo report `Package lookup failures` for the\nperf-runner image (`Could not determine new digest for update`). The\nperf workflows pin the image by digest only, so Renovate looks for the\n`latest` tag, which `jdx/perf-runner` never publishes (it only pushes\n`jdx-perf-v1`), and gets a 404.\n\nThe pin now names the published tag as well:\n\n```yaml\nimage: ghcr.io/jdx/perf-runner:jdx-perf-v1@sha256:5263c143…\n```\n\nThe digest is unchanged, so the image the perf jobs run does not change.\nRenovate can now follow the `jdx-perf-v1` tag and open a PR when the\nimage is rebuilt.\n\nThe shared preset automerges digest updates, so this also adds a package\nrule that turns automerge off for `ghcr.io/jdx/perf-runner`. A rebuilt\nimage changes the toolchain every perf baseline is measured on, and that\nshould go through the perf check, not merge on its own.\n\nThe `image:` strings that the workflows echo into the report are left as\nthey were.\n\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Claude Code; model: Anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5;\nversion: unavailable.*\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> CI and Renovate config only; the perf-runner digest is unchanged so\nmeasured environments stay the same.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Perf CI now pins the benchmark container as\n`ghcr.io/jdx/perf-runner:jdx-perf-v1@sha256:…` in **measure** and\n**perf-pr** instead of digest-only. The digest is unchanged, so jobs\nstill run the same image; adding the published `jdx-perf-v1` tag lets\nRenovate resolve updates instead of failing on a missing `latest` tag.\n> \n> **renovate.json** adds a package rule that disables automerge for\n`ghcr.io/jdx/perf-runner`, so image rebuilds (and toolchain changes)\nrequire review and perf validation rather than merging from the shared\npreset alone.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n02b926a327561c47b986041f7df87f47eab5e7c8. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Chores**\n* Updated the performance testing environment’s image reference; its\npinned version remains unchanged.\n* Performance testing toolchain updates now require review rather than\nbeing merged automatically.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9fa00f513ae6861ffe999fd7322af2a28b69fa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/git/trees/e9fa00f513ae6861ffe999fd7322af2a28b69fa4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/git/commits/2436db43982689b99b9a0e5794919398404e034f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq0rQ0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmv8QAIM78R/SYwjWLDovrJXle+8W\nHyRM7sHUi1S/LNApqz906HwB7RIv40ZVuKOpPuVmbUIWS9XgPd9oUSpz/dswxsib\nIrPDC0S7UJsMe5/wHoWPWPpuvSBD83qmNZXc4Ymd2zyPr4kmSmk8w/kLb7Pje+7I\nRj+dVZVybvx8wfdMtyR7V4r9MC/NSMBI/xS