ude-sonnet-5-5;\nversion: unavailable.*\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> CI and Renovate config only; the perf-runner digest is unchanged so\nmeasured environments stay the same.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Perf CI now pins the benchmark container as\n`ghcr.io/jdx/perf-runner:jdx-perf-v1@sha256:…` in **measure** and\n**perf-pr** instead of digest-only. The digest is unchanged, so jobs\nstill run the same image; adding the published `jdx-perf-v1` tag lets\nRenovate resolve updates instead of failing on a missing `latest` tag.\n> \n> **renovate.json** adds a package rule that disables automerge for\n`ghcr.io/jdx/perf-runner`, so image rebuilds (and toolchain changes)\nrequire review and perf validation rather than merging from the shared\npreset alone.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n02b926a327561c47b986041f7df87f47eab5e7c8. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Chores**\n* Updated the performance testing environment’s image reference; its\npinned version remains unchanged.\n* Performance testing toolchain updates now require review rather than\nbeing merged automatically.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-16T23:33:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/2436db43982689b99b9a0e5794919398404e034f","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/commit/2436db43982689b99b9a0e5794919398404e034f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/2436db43982689b99b9a0e5794919398404e034f/comments","author":{"login":"jdx","id":216188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjE4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0423391d49a1d2eecb976b1b25ed51cd76de7f0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/0423391d49a1d2eecb976b1b25ed51cd76de7f0c","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/commit/0423391d49a1d2eecb976b1b25ed51cd76de7f0c"}]},{"sha":"1725bbe70a76ac3f1e2fc72bf1420ae376e9399c","node_id":"C_kwDOT-nLJdoAKDE3MjViYmU3MGE3NmFjM2YxZTJmYzcyYmYxNDIwYWUzNzZlOTM5OWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jdx","email":"216188+jdx@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-17T02:01:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-17T02:01:17Z"},"message":"fix(cli): report build.rustc-wrapper = \"mbx\" instead of failing with -Zscript (#727)\n\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/jdx/mr-boxington/trails/179\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\nFixes #726.\n\nWith `build.rustc-wrapper = \"mbx\"` in Cargo configuration, every `cargo\ninstall` failed (for example `mise install cargo:*` tools) with an error\nthat never mentions the wrapper:\n\n```\nerror: running the file `.../bin/rustc` requires `-Zscript`\n```\n\nCargo runs a configured wrapper as `mbx <rustc> <args>`, and mbx handed\nthe rustc path to Cargo as a subcommand. mbx already sets\n`RUSTC_WRAPPER` for each build, so this setting is unsupported. mbx now\ndetects the call and fails with:\n\n```\nmbx[error]: mbx is configured as Cargo's rustc wrapper (`build.rustc-wrapper`, `RUSTC_WRAPPER`, or `CARGO_BUILD_RUSTC_WRAPPER`), which it does not support.\nRemove that setting: mbx sets `RUSTC_WRAPPER` for each build itself.\n```\n\nDetection covers `mbx <path>/rustc ...` and, because Cargo passes a bare\n`rustc` when `RUSTC` is unset, `mbx rustc` followed by a compiler-only\nargument such as `-vV`, `--print`, `--crate-name`, or an `@argfile`.\nOther `mbx rustc ...` calls still reach `cargo rustc`. Detection is best\neffort: an unrecognized form keeps the old error.\n\nValidation: a unit test covers the argument matching, and an integration\ntest runs real `cargo build` with the wrapper configured and checks for\nthe new message instead of `-Zscript`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Claude Code; model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5;\nversion: unavailable.*\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Early-exit guard and heuristic argv detection only; no change to\nnormal rustc shim or session `RUSTC_WRAPPER` behavior when the\nmisconfiguration is absent.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> When Cargo is configured to use **mbx** as `build.rustc-wrapper` (or\nequivalent `RUSTC_WRAPPER` / `CARGO_BUILD_RUSTC_WRAPPER`), builds used\nto fail with Cargo’s misleading `-Zscript` error because mbx treated the\ncompiler path as a CLI subcommand.\n> \n> **mbx** now detects Cargo’s wrapper invocation shape (`mbx\n<path>/rustc …` or `mbx rustc` with compiler-style flags) very early in\nstartup—before the rustc shim path—and exits with an explicit error\ntelling users to remove that setting, since mbx already sets\n`RUSTC_WRAPPER` per session. Deliberate `mbx rustc …` / `cargo rustc`\nflows are left alone via conservative argument matching.\n> \n> Coverage includes unit tests for the matcher and a Unix integration\ntest that runs a real `cargo build` with `build.rustc-wrapper` and\nexpects the new message instead of `-Zscript`.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n7d70cdf65507e0ea050d62851be41aa0fa58dd18. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Added a clear error when `mbx` is configured as Cargo’s Rust compiler\nwrapper, preventing builds from proceeding with that unsupported\nconfiguration.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"729243becd07bd4eba32b2e643e5b16b6b06d303","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/git/trees/729243becd07bd4eba32b2e643e5b16b6b06d303"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/git/commits/1725bbe70a76ac3f1e2fc72bf1420ae376e9399c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq0tbtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7+oQAG036G9qP50lGg9kegYlIRn0\nyRER3Bwc3jFHg7NfVOfLMMcV32jaQmIIKw3tJMtVxqfClJVWORgtYkrnodeG/FkU\nR+zaVIdv8utETWh1Mej9YKMxC1zoiYW8vvXU28+7327DArnDplGDqELkEWibD1Zk\nhmZN4oX6m1Gfai17pDzvMEhq6qzeUYeqSsP9o2fITrA0cqR6boH54Z53ydFTY2Qa\nizVer0I/B8UBvE+J5eag4hbr4NQKvQYMGQynE0le/aOATqLwGYKvYItN+EYTxDDs\ntFuJCN2VPEm8ripfi2o+FnTE7kc6CD+xTZSD6uye3NOmdRzB4uBRVQcytlu2WSuG\nNaC2qQZe/ytJNirRBZbpEQ29Q1yEhWPeAShrGHwaqA2IxVmk97hNLBK5twco9FxP\nSVpultINhfT0iZoj2dhoyZTRer5ViyAaN5K/KeapoHn//4RApPScwWgZWet98KOl\nEw/yF6OzgAcmocyE+8hkoS+8SIsfFTYRadUeQAvucZ8BSHrEvKgKpxFolRK8lYzY\nW4EjhNLsa14p3OCp2Vxbag+I4OFKFvzKOqu5BuT6V1xoRPdnhahoND3pleuoHAlp\nvv/T50odlDDOxWqyuqtBaLOCyPlH2G17cm0uFsSgHexi/dL5dRBVL8Ggcxo/SITo\nL6VGZOTAt+XcdAfKwDGM\n=oojm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 729243becd07bd4eba32b2e643e5b16b6b06d303\nparent 2436db43982689b99b9a0e5794919398404e034f\nauthor jdx <216188+jdx@users.noreply.github.com> 1792202477 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792202477 +0000\n\nfix(cli): report build.rustc-wrapper = \"mbx\" instead of failing with -Zscript (#727)\n\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/jdx/mr-boxington/trails/179\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\nFixes #726.\n\nWith `build.rustc-wrapper = \"mbx\"` in Cargo configuration, every `cargo\ninstall` failed (for example `mise install cargo:*` tools) with an error\nthat never mentions the wrapper:\n\n```\nerror: running the file `.../bin/rustc` requires `-Zscript`\n```\n\nCargo runs a configured wrapper as `mbx <rustc> <args>`, and mbx handed\nthe rustc path to Cargo as a subcommand. mbx already sets\n`RUSTC_WRAPPER` for each build, so this setting is unsupported. mbx now\ndetects the call and fails with:\n\n```\nmbx[error]: mbx is configured as Cargo's rustc wrapper (`build.rustc-wrapper`, `RUSTC_WRAPPER`, or `CARGO_BUILD_RUSTC_WRAPPER`), which it does not support.\nRemove that setting: mbx sets `RUSTC_WRAPPER` for each build itself.\n```\n\nDetection covers `mbx <path>/rustc ...` and, because Cargo passes a bare\n`rustc` when `RUSTC` is unset, `mbx rustc` followed by a compiler-only\nargument such as `-vV`, `--print`, `--crate-name`, or an `@argfile`.\nOther `mbx rustc ...` calls still reach `cargo rustc`. Detection is best\neffort: an unrecognized form keeps the old error.\n\nValidation: a unit test covers the argument matching, and an integration\ntest runs real `cargo build` with the wrapper configured and checks for\nthe new message instead of `-Zscript`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Claude Code; model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5;\nversion: unavailable.*\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Early-exit guard and heuristic argv detection only; no change to\nnormal rustc shim or session `RUSTC_WRAPPER` behavior when the\nmisconfiguration is absent.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> When Cargo is configured to use **mbx** as `build.rustc-wrapper` (or\nequivalent `RUSTC_WRAPPER` / `CARGO_BUILD_RUSTC_WRAPPER`), builds used\nto fail with Cargo’s misleading `-Zscript` error because mbx treated the\ncompiler path as a CLI subcommand.\n> \n> **mbx** now detects Cargo’s wrapper invocation shape (`mbx\n<path>/rustc …` or `mbx rustc` with compiler-style flags) very early in\nstartup—before the rustc shim path—and exits with an explicit error\ntelling users to remove that setting, since mbx already sets\n`RUSTC_WRAPPER` per session. Deliberate `mbx rustc …` / `cargo rustc`\nflows are left alone via conservative argument matching.\n> \n> Coverage includes unit tests for the matcher and a Unix integration\ntest that runs a real `cargo build` with `build.rustc-wrapper` and\nexpects the new message instead of `-Zscript`.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n7d70cdf65507e0ea050d62851be41aa0fa58dd18. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Added a clear error when `mbx` is configured as Cargo’s Rust compiler\nwrapper, preventing builds from proceeding with that unsupported\nconfiguration.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-17T02:01:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/1725bbe70a76ac3f1e2fc72bf1420ae376e9399c","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/commit/1725bbe70a76ac3f1e2fc72bf1420ae376e9399c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/1725bbe70a76ac3f1e2fc72bf1420ae376e9399c/comments","author":{"login":"jdx","id":216188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjE4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2436db43982689b99b9a0e5794919398404e034f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/commits/2436db43982689b99b9a0e5794919398404e034f","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/commit/2436db43982689b99b9a0e5794919398404e034f"}]},{"sha":"2791d50164783a0a5562bca848b47c93fe71392a","node_id":"C_kwDOT-nLJdoAKDI3OTFkNTAxNjQ3ODNhMGE1NTYyYmNhODQ4YjQ3YzkzZmU3MTM5MmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"renovate[bot]","email":"29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-17T12:34:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-17T12:34:53Z"},"message":"chore(deps): update jdx crates (#729)\n\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/jdx/mr-boxington/trails/180\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\nThis PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Type | Update | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [demand](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/demand) | dependencies |\npatch | `2.4.0` → `2.4.1` |\n| [usage-rs](https://usage.jdx.dev)\n([source](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/usage)) | dependencies | patch\n| `7.0.1` → `7.0.2` |\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>jdx/demand (demand)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v2.4.1`](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/demand/blob/HEAD/CHANGELOG.md#241---2026-10-17)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/demand/compare/v2.4.0...v2.4.1)\n\n##### Fixed\n\n- clippy for all-targets, empty-filter selection perf, and input\nCtrl-N/Ctrl-P\n([#&#8203;249](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/demand/pull/249))\n\n##### Other\n\n- *(release-plz)* use the image's rust instead of dtolnay/rust-toolchain\n([#&#8203;250](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/demand/pull/250))\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>jdx/usage (usage-rs)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v7.0.2`](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/usage/blob/HEAD/CHANGELOG.md#702---2026-10-16)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/usage/compare/v7.0.1...v7.0.2)\n\n##### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n\n- **(complete)** read .<script>.usage.kdl sidecar when completing\nscripts by [@&#8203;jdx](https://redirect.github.com/jdx) in\n[#&#8203;1558](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/usage/pull/1558)\n- **(complete)** show help for short flag completions by\n[@&#8203;Ehsan-hash](https://redirect.github.com/Ehsan-hash) in\n[#&#8203;1561](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/usage/pull/1561)\n\n##### 🛡️ Security\n\n- replace prettier with oxfmt by\n[@&#8203;jdx](https://redirect.github.com/jdx) in\n[#&#8203;1560](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/usage/pull/1560)\n\n##### 🔍 Other Changes\n\n- **(release)** shorten minimum release age to 2 days by\n[@&#8203;jdx](https://redirect.github.com/jdx) in\n[52b1b78](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/usage/commit/52b1b7874590f2e6d5becaa86d0395647dce7991)\n- pin perf-runner image by tag and stop automerging it by\n[@&#8203;jdx](https://redirect.github.com/jdx) in\n[#&#8203;1562](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/usage/pull/1562)\n\n##### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;Ehsan-hash](https://redirect.github.com/Ehsan-hash) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;1561](https://redirect.github.com/jdx/usage/pull/1561)\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Configuration\n\n📅 **Schedule**: (in timezone America/Chicago)\n\n- Branch creation\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n- Automerge\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n\n🚦 **Automerge**: Enabled.\n\n♻ **Rebasing**: Whenever PR becomes conflicted, or you tick the\nrebase/retry checkbox.\n\n👻 **Immortal**: This PR will be recreated if closed unmerged. Get\n[config\nhelp](https://redirect.github.com/renovatebot/renovate/discussions) if\nthat's undesired.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] <!-- rebase-check -->If you want to rebase/retry this PR, check\nthis box\n\n---\n\nThis PR was generated by [Mend Renovate](https://mend.io/renovate/).\nView the [repository job\nlog](https://developer.mend.io/github/jdx/mr-boxington).\n\n<!--renovate-debug:eyJjcmVhdGVkSW5WZXIiOiI0NC4xNjQuMSIsInVwZGF0ZWRJblZlciI6IjQ0LjE2NC4xIiwidGFyZ2V0QnJhbmNoIjoibWFpbiIsImxhYmVscyI6W119-->\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"827716b758bcc762f33e4986654c485dd0ec26db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/git/trees/827716b758bcc762f33e4986654c485dd0ec26db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mr-boxington/git/commits/2791d50164783a0a5562bca848b47c93fe71392a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq02ttCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxLoQAEvS0N17PInnphRqQ+dJVHod\nNXFX6+LZCm/V8WgwtS0HqCpMiFX8WchOI+ZacfZcTRny34/WhZDP2okxE8ektdUF\nqwQGp7goSDYsUGvd7ncBGv3Urso0E5PsvAwbW32H/IO4h3KYVPuMSBYp2VNKoBDb\nMfgGv0NPjoDyjxLQjPgCI1Odsg74EVSh7Z8Y+TH7EXf4dDxa3ELSyyjJk3fIvN94\n3QyFV7Qf+RAKIPa5tWsUmPywmjURXaajs4UAl+OicVvcGS721JoCtYS+fhKXzDRN\nogCWsLgY+bn571gsxfBWcS0JXw7X6Re4fxeUrybo85Ve8RyDcimmPc7gY+EQ3Rv4\nAsfXo9CUnp2CQc+UuCUEKbt2PBW0t7TLV5KnIZtgmA05xJjnQP9IM9mqisKvvqhJ\nCutQeNvfXxOaQrWoVY5zcbUtRQWVLxjn2sk63BpbXUEU9uDUd670qFWI+wMKV/BF\n120BJJaSb8uKv00nCCCa2bdWfznBlt5xm+eM835dk0ttV0T9aUj31oC3nDhUnzFO\nMxEr7CiMIcxm3e+L7c7oGBI5aMRw+jr6cF3FQ+gEwTPRRT+0St83GCv6QXCTLVZT\n22x6JheJLEtxt